---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import dataset from '../../public/data/mcp_servers.json';
import { fmt } from '../lib/format';

const activeCount = dataset.count;
const totalCount = dataset.count_including_delisted;
const generatedAt = (dataset as any).generated_at;

const canonicalPath = '/data';
const canonicalUrl = new URL(canonicalPath, Astro.site).toString().replace(/\/$/, '');

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: 'MCP Junction — MCP Server Directory',
  description: 'A structured, nightly-updated directory of Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers, derived from the public GitHub REST API. Contains server metadata, licenses, install hints, and category assignments.',
  url: canonicalUrl,
  dateModified: generatedAt,
  license: 'https://mcpjunction.ai/licensing',
  creator: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'MCP Junction',
    url: 'https://mcpjunction.ai',
  },
  distribution: [
    {
      '@type': 'DataDownload',
      encodingFormat: 'application/json',
      contentUrl: 'https://mcpjunction.ai/data/mcp_servers.json',
    },
    {
      '@type': 'DataDownload',
      encodingFormat: 'text/csv',
      contentUrl: 'https://mcpjunction.ai/data/mcp_servers.csv',
    },
  ],
};
---
<Base
  title="Dataset — MCP Junction"
  description={`Downloadable dataset of ${activeCount} MCP servers, refreshed nightly from the public GitHub REST API. Available as JSON and CSV.`}
  canonical={canonicalPath}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
<h1>Dataset</h1>
<p>MCP Junction publishes its full directory as machine-readable data, refreshed nightly. Every server page on this site is derived from this dataset.</p>

<h2>Downloads</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Format</th><th>URL</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
  <tr>
    <td>JSON</td>
    <td><a href="/data/mcp_servers.json">/data/mcp_servers.json</a></td>
    <td>Envelope with metadata + full <code>servers</code> array. Canonical form.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>CSV</td>
    <td><a href="/data/mcp_servers.csv">/data/mcp_servers.csv</a></td>
    <td>Flat rows for spreadsheet import. Formula-injection guarded per OWASP.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>At a glance</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Active servers</th><td>{fmt(activeCount)}</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Total including delisted (30-day grace)</th><td>{fmt(totalCount)}</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Last generated</th><td>{generatedAt}</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Source</th><td>GitHub REST API (public repository metadata) + editorial review</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Refresh cadence</th><td>Nightly, ~06:17 UTC</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Query it as an MCP server</h2>
<p>This directory is itself an MCP server. Point your agent at
<code>https://mcpjunction.ai/mcp</code> (streamable HTTP, stateless, no auth)
and it can search the directory with <code>search_servers</code> (by keyword,
category, or GitHub topic), fetch one entry with <code>get_server</code>, and
browse with <code>list_categories</code> and <code>list_topics</code>. Claude
Code example:</p>
<pre class="block"><code>claude mcp add --transport http mcpjunction https://mcpjunction.ai/mcp</code></pre>

<h2>Licensing</h2>
<p>Directory content is licensed per <a href="/licensing">/licensing</a>. In brief:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Web search indexing — free</li>
  <li>Agent / inference-time retrieval of pages — free during launch, with attribution ("via mcpjunction.ai")</li>
  <li>Bulk retrieval of this dataset — requires a license</li>
  <li>AI model training on this content — requires a paid license</li>
</ul>
<p>See <a href="/license.xml">/license.xml</a> for machine-readable RSL terms.</p>

<h2>How to cite</h2>
<pre class="block cite"><code>MCP Junction — MCP Server Directory. {generatedAt}.
{canonicalUrl}. Data: https://mcpjunction.ai/data/mcp_servers.json.
Licensed per https://mcpjunction.ai/licensing.</code></pre>

<h2>Compliance and provenance</h2>
<p>Data is collected via the official GitHub REST API only — no HTML scraping. The pipeline republishes public GitHub owner handles with attribution and honors correction and takedown requests within 3 business days (email <a href="mailto:licensing@mcpjunction.ai">licensing@mcpjunction.ai</a>).</p>
<p class="meta">MCP Junction is not affiliated with Anthropic or the Model Context Protocol project.</p>
</Base>
